Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.35,0:00:03.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,Now, the twist. Our renter is extremely disciplined.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.68,0:00:07.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,They invest every dollar they save, every month, for
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:07.84,Cap,,0,0,0,,thirty years.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.16,0:00:11.68,Cap,,0,0,0,,What if they don't? What if that $910 a month just
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.68,0:00:12.46,Cap,,0,0,0,,gets spent?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.36,0:00:16.70,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then buying breaks even in just 2.4 years, and never
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.70,0:00:17.41,Cap,,0,0,0,,looks back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.73,0:00:20.77,Cap,,0,0,0,,This is the real reason so many homeowners end up
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.77,0:00:23.86,Cap,,0,0,0,,wealthier than renters. It's not that a house is a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.86,0:00:25.04,Cap,,0,0,0,,magical investment.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.36,0:00:28.21,Cap,,0,0,0,,It's that a mortgage is a forced savings plan, and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.21,0:00:30.49,Cap,,0,0,0,,most of us are bad at forcing ourselves.
